=== warning text
exit 2
--- stderr
[bendit] that command hid its errors and returned nothing, so it has told you nothing.
An empty result here means EITHER "ran fine, found none" OR "failed, and you cannot see why" — the two look identical and mean opposite things.
Before using this as an answer, re-run it without the redirect:
  drop 2>/dev/null and read stderr
A binary at a path where it does not exist, or a directory that is not there, fails silently this way.

=== warning text: a count of zero
exit 2
--- stderr
[bendit] that command hid its errors and returned only a count of 0, so it has told you nothing.
A 0 here means EITHER "ran fine, found none" OR "failed, and you cannot see why" — the two look identical and mean opposite things.
Before using this as an answer, re-run it without the redirect:
  drop 2>/dev/null and read stderr
A binary at a path where it does not exist, or a directory that is not there, fails silently this way.

